We are global private markets specialists delivering tailored investment solutions, advisory services, and impactful, data driven insights to the world’s investors. Leveraging the power of our platform and our peerless intelligence across sectors, strategies, and geographies, we help identify the advantages and the answers our clients need to succeed. 
 The Analyst will be an integral part of StepStone's Private Equity Secondaries investment team, which recently closed its fifth fund with $7.4 billion of total capital commitments. StepStone deploys billions of dollars per year in private equity secondary deals, including GP-led transactions, LP interests in private equity funds and structured secondary deals (e.g., team spin-outs, direct investments, fund recapitalizations and other special situations). 
 StepStone prides itself on the firm’s collegial atmosphere, encouraging team-building initiatives and a collaborative approach. The position will have exposure to all levels of the firm globally, from Partners to fellow Analysts, on a daily basis. 
 Position Overview: 
 Your main responsibility will be to contribute to all aspects of the secondary deal process, including: 
 Sourcing, screening and conducting due diligence on European private equity secondary investments (both LP and GP-led transactions); 
 Interact with management teams and fund managers to conduct in-depth asset and portfolio-level analysis;
 Perform quantitative and qualitative research and financial modelling/analysis on companies and assets across stages,  industries and geographies;
 Preparation and presentation of due diligence materials and investment committee memos;
 Construct an opinion around various investment opportunities and efficiently communicate both verbally and in written materials; with the ability to defend your position in a team environment, including investment committee meetings;
 Support negotiation/coordination of deal closing/structuring process and post-close monitoring of existing investments; and
 Occasionally travel for onsite due diligence and to sponsor’s annual meetings to monitor investments.
 Requirements: 
 Stellar academic record (university and GPA);
 1-2 years of private equity, top-tier investment banking and/or consulting experience; 
 Excellent quantitative skills, including financial modelling, analytical and valuation skills for purpose of evaluating investment opportunities;
 Strong sense of risk/reward trade-offs, and an ability to display sound investment judgement; 
 Strong appetite for self-directed learning, particularly in AI/automation, with demonstrated hands-on experimentation preferred;  
 Self-starter, with strong ability to think creativity and conduct research to solve problems or find solutions;
 Ability to communicate and present ideas effectively, both verbally and in writing;
 Capable of multi-tasking with strong attention to detail;
 Promote and demonstrate a positive, team-oriented attitude, with desire to work on various projects; and
 Fluent (written and spoken) English; (additional language skills a plus).
